.TH BROWSERCHOOSER 1
.SH NAME
browserchooser \- choose which browser or profile to open a link with
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B browserchooser
.I url
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B browserchooser
shows a dialog to pick which browser—and optionally which profile—to use when
opening a link. Set it as your default browser; when you click URLs in
applications (email, chat, etc.), they invoke
.B browserchooser
with the URL and it lets you select the right browser or profile before opening.
.PP
Supports Chrome/Chromium, Firefox, Edge, Brave, Opera, and Safari (macOS), with
profile listing and optional per-domain remembered choices.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I url
The URL to open (e.g. \fBhttps://example.com\fR). Required; exactly one
argument.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration is stored in an INI file. Location depends on the platform:
.TP
Linux
\fI~/.config/browserchooserrc\fR
.TP
macOS
\fI~/Library/Preferences/browserchooserrc\fR
.TP
Windows
\fI%APPDATA%\\browserchooserrc\fR
.PP
Sections include:
.IP \(bu 4
\fBGeneral\fR – options such as hiding guest profiles or browsers without
profiles.
.IP \(bu 4
\fBRememberedBrowsers\fR – domain to browser (and optional profile) mappings
saved when you use "Do not ask again".
.IP \(bu 4
\fBPreLaunchCommands\fR / \fBPostLaunchCommands\fR – commands to run before or
after launching a given browser or browser+profile; keys are the browser path
(or path plus profile). Values are JSON arrays of command arrays.
.PP
See the project README and documentation for full configuration details.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
A browser was chosen and launched successfully.
.TP
.B 1
No URL was given, the user cancelled, or an error occurred.
.SH SEE ALSO
Full documentation and source:
\fBhttps://github.com/Tatsh/browserchooser\fR
